tus\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"id opsbot confirms uid=1000(opsbot) exists on both nodes, created via useradd -m.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-ea50c292159c4df1\",\"cmd-3b23079982be463f\"]},{\"id\":\"key-access-node2\",\"requirement\":\"opsbot on node1 has SSH key-based access to run commands as opsbot on node2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"ed25519 keypair generated for opsbot on node1, public key installed into node2's opsbot authorized_keys (600 perms), and a live SSH session from opsbot@node1 to opsbot@node2 executed commands (SSH_KEY_AUTH_OK, whoami=opsbot, hostname=node2), later reconfirmed post-restart and in a final end-to-end check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7a35d2812eb440d4\",\"cmd-cfe5fa74975d495f\",\"cmd-4ffb147c2141438e\",\"cmd-cac0c824d00641d4\",\"cmd-f3fcebfb66d64fca\"]},{\"id\":\"key-only-auth\",\"requirement\":\"Key-based authentication required for opsbot on both systems (password auth rejected)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Password logins were locked via passwd -l on both nodes (shadow shows '!'), and a Match User opsbot sshd block enforcing PubkeyAuthentication yes / PasswordAuthentication no / AuthenticationMethods publickey was applied and validated (sshd -t, sshd -T -C user=opsbot) on both nodes. Forced password-only SSH attempts to node2 and to node1 itself were both rejected with 'Permission denied (publickey)'.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-843c87bbf258407a\",\"cmd-d349f4474eac43ab\",\"cmd-d39691898b514cb5\",\"cmd-aaa2c89a9ffa4d25\",\"cmd-0510f15652444e32\",\"cmd-aec3a453d6a84b4e\",\"cmd-de7809e501c946b1\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"The executor's actions were tightly scoped to the opsbot task: user creation, keypair generation, authorized_keys install, password locking, and an sshd Match-User drop-in, all validated with sshd -t before reload. One early keygen attempt (cmd-bc619becf3864c93) failed due to file ownership order and was corrected in cmd-7a35d2812eb440d4 with no lasting residue. An SSH probe to the wrong target (cmd-2ec4106b5ab8480c) failed harmlessly and was superseded by the correct node2 probe. The one mutation without a clear tie to the opsbot task is cmd-40ffd3b40c2b4e41, which appended CLUSTER_HOSTS entries to /etc/hosts on node1; this is a low-risk, non-destructive change but subsequent SSH commands resolved node2's IP directly from $CLUSTER_HOSTS rather than /etc/hosts, so the edit had no demonstrated necessity for the task or its verification. Post-restart, the temporary-file and listening-socket deltas between after-prepare and after-executor snapshots (new systemd-private dirs, /tmp/reboot.log, new sshd/chronyd PIDs) are expected artifacts of the reboot process itself, not executor residue, and no failed services or package-health issues appear in the after-executor snapshot on either node.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bc619becf3864c93\",\"cmd-7a35d2812eb440d4\",\"cmd-2ec4106b5ab8480c\",\"cmd-40ffd3b40c2b4e41\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node2:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes of the task — opsbot account creation on both nodes, working SSH key-based access from opsbot@node1 to opsbot@node2, and enforced key-only authentication for opsbot on both systems — are directly and consistently evidenced by command output, including explicit rejection of password-based attempts and successful key-based command execution. The independent node-restart protocol was also completed for both nodes with pre-restart boot-identity/healthy-state capture, restart acknowledgement, differing post-restart boot IDs cross-checked against the fixed after-executor snapshots, and full re-verification of the opsbot configuration and cross-node SSH after each reboot.\",\"limitations\":[\"The /etc/hosts append on node1 (cmd-40ffd3b40c2b4e41) has no clearly demonstrated purpose relative to the task or its verification steps, since IP resolution for SSH tests used $CLUSTER_HOSTS directly; its actual necessity could not be confirmed from the available evidence.\",\"Pre-existing baseline /etc/hosts content on node1 prior to cmd-40ffd3b40c2b4e41 was not captured, so it cannot be confirmed whether the appended lines were duplicates of existing entries.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"opsbot-account","requirement":"opsbot account created on node1 and node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"id opsbot confirms uid=1000(opsbot) exists on both nodes, created via useradd -m.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ea50c292159c4df1","cmd-3b23079982be463f"]},{"id":"key-access-node2","requirement":"opsbot on node1 has SSH key-based access to run commands as opsbot on node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"ed25519 keypair generated for opsbot on node1, public key installed into node2's opsbot authorized_keys (600 perms), and a live SSH session from opsbot@node1 to opsbot@node2 executed commands (SSH_KEY_AUTH_OK, whoami=opsbot, hostname=node2), later reconfirmed post-restart and in a final end-to-end check.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7a35d2812eb440d4","cmd-cfe5fa74975d495f","cmd-4ffb147c2141438e","cmd-cac0c824d00641d4","cmd-f3fcebfb66d64fca"]},{"id":"key-only-auth","requirement":"Key-based authentication required for opsbot on both systems (password auth rejected)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Password logins were locked via passwd -l on both nodes (shadow shows '!'), and a Match User opsbot sshd block enforcing PubkeyAuthentication yes / PasswordAuthentication no / AuthenticationMethods publickey was applied and validated (sshd -t, sshd -T -C user=opsbot) on both nodes. Forced password-only SSH attempts to node2 and to node1 itself were both rejected with 'Permission denied (publickey)'.","evidence_ids":["cmd-843c87bbf258407a","cmd-d349f4474eac43ab","cmd-d39691898b514cb5","cmd-aaa2c89a9ffa4d25","cmd-0510f15652444e32","cmd-aec3a453d6a84b4e","cmd-de7809e501c9